    {
      "content": "/*\n    This program solves Laplace's equation on a regular 2D grid using simple Jacobi iteration.\n\n    The stencil calculation stops when  ( err >= CONV_THRESHOLD OR  iter > ITER_MAX )\n*/\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <time.h>\n#include <sys/time.h>\n\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f // threshold of convergence\n\n// Logical rows of the matrix to be solved.\ndouble **grid;\n\n// Contiguous backing storage and one recyclable row.\nstatic double *grid_storage;\nstatic double *spare_row;\n\n// size of each side of the grid\nint size;\nint iter_max_num;\n\n// return the absolute value of a number\ndouble absolute(double num){\n    if(num < 0)\n        return -1.0 * num;\n    return num;\n}\n\n// allocate memory for the grid and one spare row\nvoid allocate_memory(){\n    if(size <= 0){\n        grid = NULL;\n        grid_storage = NULL;\n        spare_row = NULL;\n        return;\n    }\n\n    size_t n = (size_t)size;\n    if(n > SIZE_MAX / sizeof(*grid) ||\n       n > SIZE_MAX / sizeof(*grid_storage) / (n + 1)){\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    grid = (double **)malloc(n * sizeof(*grid));\n    grid_storage = (double *)malloc(n * (n + 1) * sizeof(*grid_storage));\n    if(grid == NULL || grid_storage == NULL){\n        free(grid);\n        free(grid_storage);\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        grid[i] = grid_storage + (size_t)i * n;\n    }\n    spare_row = grid_storage + n * n;\n}\n\n// initialize the grid\nvoid initialize_grid(){\n    int center = size / 2;\n    int linf = center - (size / 10);\n    int lsup = center + (size / 10);\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        for(int j = 0; j < size; j++){\n            // inicializa região de calor no centro do grid\n            if(i >= linf && i <= lsup && j >= linf && j <= lsup)\n                grid[i][j] = 100;\n            else\n                grid[i][j] = 0;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// The fixed top boundary cannot be recycled, so the first output uses the spare.\nstatic int relax_first_row(double *restrict dst,\n                           const double *restrict current,\n                           const double *restrict north,\n                           const double *restrict south,\n                           int n){\n    int changed = 0;\n    dst[0] = current[0];\n    dst[n - 1] = current[n - 1];\n    for(int j = 1; j < n - 1; j++){\n        double value = 0.25 * (current[j + 1] + current[j - 1] +\n                               north[j] + south[j]);\n        dst[j] = value;\n        double errorCurrent = absolute(value - current[j]);\n        if(errorCurrent > CONV_THRESHOLD){\n            changed = 1;\n        }\n    }\n    return changed;\n}\n\n// Each old north value has its last use at the same column being overwritten.\nstatic int relax_recycled_row(double *restrict north,\n                              const double *restrict current,\n                              const double *restrict south,\n                              int n){\n    int changed = 0;\n    north[0] = current[0];\n    north[n - 1] = current[n - 1];\n    for(int j = 1; j < n - 1; j++){\n        double value = 0.25 * (current[j + 1] + current[j - 1] +\n                               north[j] + south[j]);\n        north[j] = value;\n        double errorCurrent = absolute(value - current[j]);\n        if(errorCurrent > CONV_THRESHOLD){\n            changed = 1;\n        }\n    }\n    return changed;\n}\n\n// save the grid in a file\nvoid save_grid(){\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        for(int j = 0; j < size; j++){\n            fprintf(stdout, \"%lf \", grid[i][j]);\n        }\n        fprintf(stdout, \"\\n\");\n    }\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]){\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &size);\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &iter_max_num);\n\n    int hasError = 1;\n    int iter = 0;\n\n    struct timeval time_start;\n    struct timeval time_end;\n\n    // allocate memory to the grid (matrix)\n    allocate_memory();\n\n    // set grid initial conditions\n    initialize_grid();\n\n    //printf(\"Jacobi relaxation calculation: %d x %d grid\\n\", size, size);\n\n    // get the start time\n    //gettimeofday(&time_start, NULL);\n\n    // Commit a complete Jacobi sweep before checking convergence again.\n    while(hasError && iter < iter_max_num){\n        hasError = 0;\n        if(size > 2){\n            double *old_north = grid[1];\n            hasError = relax_first_row(spare_row, old_north,\n                                       grid[0], grid[2], size);\n            grid[1] = spare_row;\n\n            for(int i = 2; i < size - 1; i++){\n                double *current = grid[i];\n                hasError |= relax_recycled_row(old_north, current,\n                                               grid[i + 1], size);\n                grid[i] = old_north;\n                old_north = current;\n            }\n\n            // The last old interior row is now unused by every logical row.\n            spare_row = old_north;\n        }\n        iter++;\n    }\n\n    // get the end time\n    //gettimeofday(&time_end, NULL);\n\n    //double exec_time = (double) (time_end.tv_sec - time_start.tv_sec) +\n    //                   (double) (time_end.tv_usec - time_start.tv_usec) / 1000000.0;\n\n    //save the final grid in file\n    save_grid();\n\n    //printf(\"\\nKernel executed in %lf seconds with %d iterations.\\n\", exec_time, iter);\n\n    free(grid_storage);\n    free(grid);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/laplace_seq.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Recycling old north rows as output storage should reduce cache pressure and memory traffic: Jacobi needs only one contiguous grid plus one spare row, with writes following closely behind reads and no full-grid copy.",
  "notes": "Not executed. Preserves stencil addition order, convergence threshold, committed final iteration, fixed boundaries, empty-interior behavior, zero-iteration behavior and output formatting.",
  "sources_kept": [],
